      "side": 1,
      "message": "I checked in on this change to see if generic EC support was far enough along to land this now. It seems not to be. Though the change at [1] is landed, enabling _POWERSEQ leads to lots of undefined GPIOs, including GPIO_EN_PP5000, GPIO_PCH_SLP_S3_L, GPIO_PCH_SLP_S0_L, GPIO_CPU_PROCHOT, GPIO_PG_EC_RSMRST_ODL, GPIO_PCH_RSMRST_L, GPIO_SYS_RESET_L, and others.\n\nKeith, any idea when these GPIOs are going to get defined for Nissa boards? CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_POWERSEQ is a pretty core config, I\u0027m a little surprised it\u0027s not on yet.\n\n\n[1] https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/3449792/3",
